> PARSER EXPECTED: "]"

Note that C = 3 and theta is length 4, so something like  theta[2:C+1] is called for. I also tried theta[2:4] and
theta[2:(C+1)], and got the same error message.

Grazie for staying with me on this.

Best,
John

On Fri, Apr 1, 2016 at 10:54 AM, Bob Carpenter <ca...@alias-i.com> wrote:

> I missed this the first time around, but to answer your efficiency issues,
> see below.
>
> Change this:
>
>   for (c in 1:C){
>     for (j in 1:J){
>       eb0[c,j] <- z[j] * b0[c];
>     }
>
> to
>
>   for (c in 1:C)
>     eb0[c] <- z * b0[c];
>
> It'll vectorize the scalar multiplications.  And change this
>
>  for (c in 1:C){
>     for (j in 1:J){
>       a0[c,j] ~ normal(eb0[c,j], sigma[c]);
>     }
>   }
>
> to
>
>  for (c in 1:C)
>    a0[c] ~ normal(eb0[c], sigma[c]);
>
> That'll be a big win.  As will be changing this
>
>   for (c in 1:C){
>     b0[c] ~ normal(0, 10);
>   }
>
> to
>
>   b0 ~ normal(0, 10);
>
> Finally, change this:
>
>  for ( i in 1:N ) {
>     for (c in 1:C){
>       s[i,c] <- a0[c,id[i]] + x[i] * b[c] ;
>       theta[1] <- 0;
>       theta[c+1] <- s[i,c];
>     }
>     y[i] ~ categorical_logit(theta);
>   }
>
> to
>
>   theta[1] <- 0;
>   for (n in 1:N)
>     theta[2:C] <- a0[1:C, id[i]] + x[i] * b;
>     y[n] ~ categorical_logit(theta);
>   }
>
> I only looked at the first file, but hopefully you see the pattern.
>
> - Bob
