Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

> I just keep the model I select (i.e., the posterior over k has collapsed onto a single model). This is probably bad...
> As a possibly better alternative, I can build a rough estimate of the posterior over k based on the exponentiated PSIS-LOO CV score of each k (similar to what Burnham & Anderson suggest for AIC-weighted prediction).

PS: I see why (1) would not work. If a LOO posterior ends up selecting a different model than the full posterior, then there is no overlap between posteriors, and clearly IS would not work.
However, as bad as it can be, (2) would not have this problem. Perhaps I wouldn't even need to actually sample k, I could use the formula of the pseudo-posterior when needed, although I haven't thought about the maths in detail.

