> I am pretty new to rstanarm and multilevel modelling (and this might sound pretty silly to you), but in some instances when running a stan_glmer model I have come across a _NEW_ intercept in the output (see below in bold). What is this term exactly?

It is the posterior distribution distribution of the parameter(s) for a new level of the grouping term(s). In your case, if there were an eighth SUPPLIER1, it would have an intercept shift that is normal with mean zero and standard deviation 0.123.

Ben

