You can make the eigenvalues and eigenvectors parameters and theta goes into transformed parameters.  The eigenvalues should have priors between -1 and 1 and each column of the right (?) Eigenvectors can be a simplex. If you use a sort on the eigenvalues parameters you can assure the first is the largest and the corresponding eigenvector can be the simplex that corresponds to the stationary distribution you want to put priors on.  I've thought about this more for VAR models than for HMM so I'm not sure I have all the details right.

