That's only happening a few times, hence the (rather rude) message
at the end of the warning message.  Feel free to write in about whatever
you want, but the answer's probably going to be that if this only
happens a few times, it's not a big deal.

You can often remove these problems by setting a smaller initial
stepsize and higher target acceptance control=list(stepsize=0.01, adapt_delta=0.99).
Maybe .95 would be enough.

You might provide a more informative prior parameter alpha (don't
know what it is now).

- Bob

