Thanks,

In my little experience these numerical instabilities (although happen few time per chain) degrade the sampling efficiency and always hide (in my case) bad modelling choices of bugs in the model, that I was always able to correct.

Maybe it is helpful to specify that the step that cause the invalid simplex is the  multiplication by the "perturbation" parameter. That has a gamma prior.

A more precise question is:

Since the problem is the perturbation parameter, how can I know what values assume at the iterations that cause those 9 warnings? And what is then the value of phi_hat?

Does it assume all 0? All infinite? A negative value?

The reason why I put my issue here that I don't know the tools to troubleshoot this, understanding all values of these two parameters at the time of the simplex error.

I thought that some may have recognized the numerical cause of this issue.

Thanks.

